# Marina's monument on the dry mound, the vault beneath it, and Strahd's visit by night (docs/regions/berez.md §3.1).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The statue (prop on the mound)

~ monument
Narrator: On the only dry ground in Berez stands a young woman in white stone, her hands folded, her face turned toward the castle. Someone has scrubbed the moss from her. At her feet lie fresh black roses, and an iron grave-lamp, unlit.
if guest:ireena and not flag.ireena_saw_marina
set ireena_saw_marina
cutscene marina_statue
Narrator: Ireena stops at the foot of the mound. The statue has her face. Not a likeness: her face, the set of the jaw, the small frown.
Ireena: I've never been here. I know I've never been here. So why do I know there are nine steps under that plinth?
endif
-> monument_menu

~ monument_menu
* Read the plinth. -> plinth
* [if not flag.marina_vault_found] Dig around the plinth. -> dig
* [if not flag.marina_lamp_lit] Light the grave-lamp at her feet. -> lamp
* Leave her in peace. -> END

~ plinth
Narrator: One word is cut deep into the plinth: MARINA. Below it, smaller, in the same fine and patient hand: Berez took her. I took Berez.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: He signed it. Like a receipt. So he does sign things. Good to know. No reason.
else
interject tag:pious: He signed it. He signed a grave, the way you'd sign a letter.
endif
-> monument_menu

~ dig
set marina_vault_found
time +30
Narrator: Half an hour of scraping silt and pulling reeds bares a slab at the foot of the plinth with an iron ring in it. Under the slab, a stair goes down into the mound, perfectly dry, and somewhere below it a candle is burning.
if guest:ireena
Ireena: Nine steps.
endif
-> monument_menu

~ lamp
set marina_lamp_lit
Narrator: The wick takes at once, as if it had been waiting. A small, steady yellow light stands on the mound in the middle of the black marsh, where everything can see it.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You lit Marina's grave-lamp
if flag.lysaga_dead or flag.lysaga_left_broken or flag.strahd_knows_marina_truth
Narrator: Nothing answers it but the frogs. For a while the statue's face looks almost warm.
-> END
endif
Narrator: Out in the east, a shutter bangs. A scream comes across the reeds, thin and rising, the scream of someone who has seen a light where no light should be.
cutscene lysaga_bowl
Baba Lysaga [angry]: WHO LIT HER LAMP? Who lit that little cat's lamp? I'll have your eyes for candles!
set lysaga_lured
if not quest.the_witch_of_berez
quest the_witch_of_berez arrived
endif
combat lysaga_at_monument

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Marina's bier (prop in the vault)

~ bier
Narrator: She lies on a bier of white stone under a veil of lace, a girl of perhaps nineteen, with red hair braided over one shoulder. She looks asleep. She has looked asleep for a very long time. There is no smell at all.
if guest:ireena
Narrator: Ireena stands at the foot of the bier and doesn't move. The girl on it has her face, too.
Ireena: He keeps finding us. Doesn't he. Over and over, he keeps finding us, and it never ends well for the girl.
endif
-> bier_menu

~ bier_menu
* [Medicine DC 14] Look, gently, for how she died. -> bier_medicine | bier_medicine_fail
* [if (flag.berez_diary_read or flag.marina_body_examined) and not flag.marina_truth_known] [Arcana DC 14] A scratch like a thorn's and nothing else. Is that a witch's death? -> bier_deduce | bier_deduce_fail
* Straighten her veil, and go. -> bier_veil
* Leave her as she is. -> END

~ bier_medicine
set marina_body_examined
Narrator: No wound, no bruise, no poison's colour in the lips. Only, above her heart, a single red scratch, fine as a bramble's, that has never healed in all this time.
-> bier_menu

~ bier_medicine_fail
Narrator: She is too perfect to read. Whatever killed her left her exactly as he wanted to remember her.
-> bier_menu

~ bier_deduce
set marina_truth_known
if not quest.the_witch_of_berez >= truth
quest the_witch_of_berez truth
endif
Narrator: A scratch that never heals, over the heart, and no hand laid on her: that is the mark a doll leaves when a thorn goes through it. Somebody in this marsh knows how to make that kind of doll, and lives on a stump.
-> bier_menu

~ bier_deduce_fail
Narrator: It could be anything. In Barovia, it usually is.
-> bier_menu

~ bier_veil
Narrator: The lace is soft and cold. When you step back, it lies a little straighter than he left it. You suspect he'll notice.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You straightened Marina's veil
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strahd at the monument (night, approach)

~ strahd
set berez_strahd_met
cutscene marina_rose
Narrator: Someone is standing at the foot of the statue with a black rose in his gloved hand. He lays it down with the others before he turns, so that you know you are less important than the rose.
if flag.strahd_met
Strahd: My guests. You do get everywhere. I am not sure I like you being here, of all places.
else
Strahd: Good evening. You will be the strangers my wolves keep telling me about. I am Strahd von Zarovich, and this is a private grave.
endif
if guest:ireena
Strahd: Ireena. You came to see her. Of course you did.
Ireena [angry]: I don't know her.
Strahd: You did once. You will again.
endif
-> strahd_menu

~ strahd_menu
* Who was she? -> strahd_who
* [Insight DC 15] Watch his face while he looks at her. -> strahd_insight | strahd_insight_fail
* [if flag.marina_truth_known and not flag.lysaga_dead] Berez didn't kill her. Your nurse did. -> strahd_truth
* [if flag.marina_truth_known and flag.lysaga_dead] The witch who killed her is dead. We saw to it. -> strahd_truth_dead
* We'll leave you with her. -> strahd_bye

~ strahd_who
Strahd: A candlemaker's daughter, which is to say nobody, which is to say someone I had looked for over a very long time. She was frightened of me. They usually are, at first.
Strahd: The village hid her from me, and in the morning she was dead in their chapel. So I sent the river to ask them why. It is still asking.
-> strahd_menu

~ strahd_insight
Narrator: The grief is real. So is the other thing under it, which isn't love so much as a collector's anger at a broken piece. He mourns her the way a man mourns a thing he owned.
-> strahd_menu

~ strahd_insight_fail
Narrator: His face is a beautiful closed door.
-> strahd_menu

~ strahd_truth
set strahd_knows_marina_truth
if not quest.the_witch_of_berez >= strahd_told
quest the_witch_of_berez strahd_told
endif
Narrator: He doesn't answer at once. The frogs stop. The wind stops. The flame in the grave-lamp, if it is lit, lies down flat.
Strahd: Explain.
Player: A doll of red hair over her hearth, with a thorn through its heart. She kept it. She still handles it.
Strahd: She sang to me, when I was small. She was the only one who did.
Strahd: Thank you. That was courageous, and very foolish, and I shall remember both. Now go home, all of you. I have to see to my house.
Narrator: He is not there any more. Out in the east, a long way off, something made of timber begins to scream.
-> END

~ strahd_truth_dead
set strahd_knows_marina_truth
Strahd: Dead. Lysaga. And you tell me she did this.
Narrator: For a long moment he looks east, toward the stump, as if he could kill her again from here and is considering it.
Strahd: Then you have done my work for me without asking, which I will forgive once. Do not let it become a habit.
-> END

~ strahd_bye
Strahd: Do. And mind the lamp, if you lit it. She never liked the dark.
-> END
